# Keep LF line endings on the shell scripts that drive local testing and that
# are baked into the Docker image, on every platform. Without this, a Windows
# checkout with the common `core.autocrlf=true` default rewrites them to CRLF,
# which breaks the `#!/usr/bin/env bash` shebang (run_tests.sh) and makes the
# container fail to start (a CRLF ENTRYPOINT script is not executable inside
# the Linux image).
#
# Scoped to the two files this matters for. Upstream Odoo shell scripts and the
# Dockerfile are intentionally left to git's default handling so nothing else
# is renormalized.
/run_tests.sh   text eol=lf
/entrypoint.sh  text eol=lf
